{"title":"Stock Photos of Muscular Men in Odd Places","link":"https://kottke.org/26/11/stock-photos-of-muscular-men-in-odd-places","date":1795129200000,"content":"\n         \t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794899188-d743dce5.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794899188-d743dce5.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794899188-d743dce5.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p><a href=\"https://freephotomuscle.com\">Muscle Plus</a> is a free stock photo site that features Japanese bodybuilders in unusual places and situations. <a href=\"https://www.tokyoweekender.com/japan-life/muscle-plus-japan-free-stock-photos-buff-men\">From Tokyo Weekender</a>:</p>\n\t<blockquote><p>There are men declaring their love in the middle of a tea plantation, men frolicking among sunflowers and men who have been abandoned in cardboard boxes, sometimes in the woods, sometimes by the roadside. The last scenario has proved popular enough to warrant an entire category, sute macho, or “abandoned buff guy,” borrowing its premise from the stray kittens left in cardboard boxes by Japanese roadsides.</p></blockquote>\n\t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794898636-10971f83.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794898636-10971f83.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794898636-10971f83.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794898677-44f6154d.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794898677-44f6154d.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794898677-44f6154d.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794898985-3b1a2603.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794898985-3b1a2603.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794898985-3b1a2603.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794899063-19a977fd.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794899063-19a977fd.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794899063-19a977fd.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p>Some of the names are great too. These two are called “The person summoned from another world wasn’t a hero, but a muscular, disposable guy” and “A muscular man who can’t fall asleep in an unfamiliar bed”:</p>\n\t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794898836-9b53815b.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794898836-9b53815b.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794898836-9b53815b.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\t<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794898853-3bb45011.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794898853-3bb45011.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none//images/posts/01/editor-1794898853-3bb45011.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n</p>\n \n\n        \n         <p><strong>Tags:</strong> <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/Japan\">Japan</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/photography\">photography</a></p>\n        \n    ","author":"Jason Kottke","siteTitle":"Kottke","siteHash":"89a883271b4598f9b33ebe87be70d38557bcd266e68aee521a8f93622e0ab723","entryHash":"e6e2eef2d918c21964f3bcf59dd13356fbf8a0e581a64b49916f0bbcab2dbe09","category":"Sites"}